# Zunia dashboard (app.zunialab.com) — environment reference
#
# Every variable the dashboard reads, with its production value when that value
# is not a secret. Copy to `.env.local` for development and override what
# differs (see "Local development" notes); never commit a filled-in copy.
#
# Two kinds of variable:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_*  inlined into the browser bundle AT BUILD TIME. Changing one
#                  needs a rebuild, and anything put here is public.
#   everything else  read by the server at runtime (a restart picks it up).
#
# Production: /srv/zunia/shared/dashboard.env on the Hetzner host, loaded by
# the systemd unit and copied to .env.production.local by zunia-infra's
# redeploy.sh before `pnpm build`. That unit also sets NODE_ENV=production,
# PORT=3012 and HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1 — do not set those here.

# --- Zunia Connect (connecting Zunia Mobile by QR code) — REQUIRED --------
# Base of the relay API (POST /v1/connect/sessions; the socket is wss on the
# same host). Build-time: it is inlined into the bundle and also added to the
# CSP connect-src (next.config.ts). Unset, the bundle falls back to
# https://api.zunialab.com (src/lib/connect/mobile.ts); set it explicitly for
# every build anyway, so the value a build ships is never an accident.
# Local development against a local zunia-backend: http://127.0.0.1:8788
NEXT_PUBLIC_ZUNIA_CONNECT_API_BASE=https://api.zunialab.com

# --- Public address (build time, optional) ----------------------------------
# The dashboard's canonical origin (src/lib/site.ts): the root layout's
# metadataBase (canonical links, og:url, share-image URLs), robots.txt's
# Sitemap line, sitemap.xml, the landing page's structured data, and the host
# printed on the share cards, the 404 page and the landing footer. Unset, it
# is https://app.zunialab.com, the production address (wallet.zunialab.com
# permanently redirects there). Only the origin is kept (no path, no trailing
# slash), and a value that is not an http(s) URL is ignored. Set it on a
# preview or staging build, so its canonical links name that host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://app.zunialab.com

# --- Market data (server-only, optional) -----------------------------------
# CoinGecko is a secondary source (market cap, supply, ATH); prices come from
# Numia, Osmosis SQS and Coinstore without a key. Unauthenticated CoinGecko
# calls from a shared IP are rate limited, so a key is recommended.
# Secret. Sent as x-cg-demo-api-key, or x-cg-pro-api-key with PLAN=pro.
COINGECKO_API_KEY=
# demo (default) or pro (uses pro-api.coingecko.com).
COINGECKO_API_PLAN=

# --- Web Push (server-only) --------------------------------------------------
# VAPID keys for RFC 8291/8292 push. Both keys or neither: without them (or
# with malformed ones) the notification settings say push is not available on
# this deployment. The public key is served at runtime by /api/push/config, so
# no rebuild is needed when it changes. Generate once:
# `pnpm exec web-push generate-vapid-keys`. The subject defaults to the value
# below; it must be a mailto: or https: URL.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Secret.
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:security@zunialab.com
# Where push subscriptions and watched addresses are stored (JSON files).
# Default `.data/` in the working directory (gitignored). Production keeps it
# outside the release so a redeploy does not drop subscriptions:
ZUNIA_DASHBOARD_DATA_DIR=/srv/zunia/shared/dashboard
# The background watcher that turns chain events into pushes starts with the
# server whenever the VAPID keys are set. `off` keeps it from starting: a
# second instance (only one process may send, or users get every push twice)
# or a laptop that has keys for testing the subscribe flow.
ZUNIA_PUSH_POLLER=

# --- Cross-chain swap venue (server-only) ----------------------------------
# Osmosis crosschain-swaps (XCS) contract. Optional: the release ships the
# production contract (label "CrossChainSwaps v1.2", code 37, verified on
# osmosis-1 2026-10-06; the address the extension pins) and uses it when this
# is unset. Set it only to move to another contract. Whatever the source, the
# address is checked against the chain (label and reviewed code id) before the
# swap engine (/api/swap/*), the route planner or the transfer tracker's
# recovery (/api/interchain/*) use it; without a verified contract the
# contract path is off and says why.
ZUNIA_XCS_CONTRACT=osmo1uwk8xc6q0s6t5qcpr6rht3sczu6du83xq8pwxjua0hfj5hzcnh3sqxwvxs
# Chains confirmed to run packet-forward-middleware / ibc-hooks, comma
# separated. Pinned answers win over the (heuristic) module probes; ibc-hooks
# registers no query service on several releases, so Osmosis probes "unknown".
ZUNIA_PFM_CHAINS=
ZUNIA_IBC_HOOKS_CHAINS=osmosis-1

# --- NFTs (CW721 / ICS721), server-only, all optional ----------------------
# Every one of these is off until set, and the NFT screens say which key is
# missing rather than guessing a value.

# Known CW721 collections to probe, per chain. CosmWasm has no chain-wide
# "tokens by owner" index, so a wallet can only ask contracts it knows about.
#   chainId=addr,addr;chainId2=addr
ZUNIA_NFT_CONTRACTS=

# A real "contracts by owner" index, where a chain has one. The only discovery
# path that can ever report a complete list. GET {url}?chainId=&owner=
# answering {"contracts": ["addr", ...]}. https:// (a loopback http URL is
# accepted in local development only). Redirects are refused.
ZUNIA_NFT_INDEXER_URL=
ZUNIA_NFT_INDEXER_NAME=

# cw-ics721 bridge contract per chain. Cross-chain NFT transfer stays off
# without it: an NFT sent to a guessed address is escrowed by nothing.
#   chainId=addr;chainId2=addr
ZUNIA_ICS721_BRIDGES=
# ICS721 channels, directional. ICS721 does not use the transfer port, so these
# cannot be discovered — they are deployment data.
#   sourceChainId>destChainId=channel-N;...
ZUNIA_ICS721_CHANNELS=

# Gateways for ipfs:// and ar:// artwork, comma separated. Each is a base path
# the content id is appended to: https only (http://127.0.0.1 in local
# development only), no credentials, no query string. There is no default on
# purpose: a hardcoded gateway would send every user's holdings to one
# operator.
ZUNIA_NFT_IPFS_GATEWAYS=
ZUNIA_NFT_ARWEAVE_GATEWAYS=

# Explorer link templates, per chain. No default: linking a user's token to a
# guessed domain is a fabrication.
#   chainId=https://host/path/{contract}/{tokenId}
ZUNIA_NFT_EXPLORER=
#   chainId=https://host/tx/{hash}
ZUNIA_EXPLORER_TX=

# Operator override for chains whose catalog row does not declare "cosmwasm"
# (the catalog carries the registry's features[] for most chains; this covers
# the rest). Set to 1 and Zunia asks such chains directly whether they run
# x/wasm instead of treating them as unsupported. Off by default.
ZUNIA_NFT_ALLOW_UNKNOWN_FEATURES=

# --- Development switches ----------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting of fan-out routes is off outside production; set to 1 to
# exercise it locally.
ZUNIA_RATE_LIMIT=

# --- Legacy (being removed; leave empty) -------------------------------------
# WalletConnect is hidden (broken end to end); Zunia Mobile connects over
# Zunia Connect above, from the Connect wallet modal. The VAPID public key moved to VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY, served
# at runtime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOBILE_DEEP_LINK=
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOBILE_UNIVERSAL_LINK=
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# --- No longer read ------------------------------------------------------------
# ZUNIA_XCS_CHAIN_ID and ZUNIA_OSMOSIS_ROUTER fed the retired
# /api/interchain/quote and /api/interchain/config routes. The venue is
# osmosis-1 and the swap engine's router endpoints ship in
# src/config/interchain.ts; drop both from dashboard.env when convenient.
# INDEXER_URL, BACKEND_URL and INDEXER_API_KEY fed the v1 proxy routes. Every
# route now reads public chain nodes and price APIs directly (zunia-indexer
# keeps no amounts and covers six chains; zunia-backend serves none of the
# paths the v1 dashboard called), so nothing in this version reads them.
# zunia-infra's redeploy.sh still writes the first two into dashboard.env;
# they are harmless there and can be dropped from it.
